  "objects": [
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "Microchip product taxonomy.",
        "term": "SAM"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 127,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:sam",
      "text": "The Atmel-lineage Microchip MCU family branding (formerly \"SMART ARM-based Microcontrollers\"). Sub-families include SAM D / D5x / E5x / L / C / G / V / S, all ARM-Cortex-M cores. CHIPS-MICROCHIP scopes to the SAM Cortex-M slice; non-SAM Microchip parts are out of scope per §11."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "This doc.",
        "term": "SAM D-class"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 128,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:sam d-class",
      "text": "The umbrella covering SAM D5x / E5x (Cortex-M4F at 120 MHz) and SAM D / SAM L / SAM C (Cortex-M0+ at 48 MHz). Used here to abstract over the part-number families when the distinction doesn't matter for IR shape."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "This doc; mirrors ESP's `pac_crate:` convention.",
        "term": "PAC crate"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 129,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:pac crate",
      "text": "Per-chip svd2rust-generated peripheral access crate, published from `atsamd-rs/atsamd`. E.g. `atsamd51j19a` v0.13.x. The Microchip chip YAML's `pac_crate:` key names the crate; `pac_version:` pins the minor version. As defined in `chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/db/chips/ATSAMD51J19A.yaml:5`; adapted: this doc adds the `pac_version:` key that the stub does not yet carry."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §15 (GCLK).",
        "term": "GCLK"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 130,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:gclk",
      "text": "Generic Clock Controller. The SAM D-class central clock multiplexer that selects one of N clock sources and divides it down to drive one or more peripheral generic-clock channels. Distinct from the PCM (Power Manager Channel) gate that controls APB / AHB clock distribution."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §16 (MCLK).",
        "term": "MCLK"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 131,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:mclk",
      "text": "Main Clock Controller (SAM D5x/E5x; the SAM D21 equivalent is **PM** — Power Manager). Owns the AHB and APBA/APBB/APBC/APBD bus clock enable masks. Asserting a peripheral's `MCLK.APBx_MASK` bit ungates its bus clock; the corresponding `GCLK.PCHCTRL` peripheral generic-clock channel ungates its functional clock. **Two-step gating** is normative for the SAM D-class — see §6 INV-MC1."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §32 (PORT).",
        "term": "PORT"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 132,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:port",
      "text": "The SAM GPIO controller. Each pad is identified by a `(group, pin)` pair (`group` 0..3 = ports A..D; `pin` 0..31). Mux selection is via the `PMUX` register (4-bit selector encoding alternate functions A..H or N). The `PINCFG` register controls input-enable / pull / drive-strength bits. CHIPS-MICROCHIP's `io_mux.rs` template emits `PORT.GROUPx.PMUX` + `PINCFG` writes."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §34 (SERCOM).",
        "term": "SERCOM"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 133,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:sercom",
      "text": "The Serial Communication peripheral block — six (D5x) or five (D21) instances per chip, each runtime-configurable as USART / I²C master / I²C slave / SPI master / SPI slave. The `mode:` field on a SERCOM instance in chip YAML names which protocol the generator emits init code for. SERCOM mode IS the IR shape's source of asymmetry vs. ESP's fixed-role peripherals (where `uart0` is always a UART)."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §25 (NVMCTRL).",
        "term": "NVMCTRL"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 134,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:nvmctrl",
      "text": "The flash controller. The chip YAML's `memory:` block names the flash region size, but bring-up code does not currently touch NVMCTRL; only its wait-state count needs configuring as a function of CPU frequency. Captured in `clocks.rs` for the D5x line, per §7."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §22 (EIC).",
        "term": "EIC"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 135,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:eic",
      "text": "External Interrupt Controller. Pin-routed interrupt source for the SAM D-class. Out of scope for CHIPS-MICROCHIP-01; the IR carries a placeholder field but emits no init code. Standards Action to extend."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "This doc.",
        "term": "MicrochipIr"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 136,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:microchipir",
      "text": "The vendor-specific intermediate representation produced by `src/bin/creator/bsp/microchip/load.rs` from the chip+board YAML pair. Parallels `EspIr` in `src/bin/creator/bsp/espressif/ir.rs`. Owned by CHIPS-MICROCHIP-01; **does not exist in repo yet**."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "This doc; mirrors ESP's emission contract.",
        "term": "template set"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 137,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:template set",
      "text": "The six MiniJinja templates the generator emits per board: `mod.rs.jinja`, `pac.rs.jinja`, `clocks.rs.jinja`, `io_mux.rs.jinja`, `peripherals.rs.jinja`, `board.rs.jinja`. Linker scripts (`memory.x.jinja`, optionally `chip.x.jinja`) are emitted alongside but counted separately. As defined in `src/bin/creator/bsp/espressif/templates/`; used without modification on filename + role."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §32.",
        "term": "PMUX function letter"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 138,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:pmux function letter",
      "text": "One of A..H (D5x) or A..N (D21 superset) naming which of the eight alternate functions a SAM pad is multiplexed to. Distinct from the ESP `iomux_fn` integer slot 0..3. The Microchip IR MUST encode this as a single-character string in the YAML, not an integer. See §6 INV-MC2."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §32.",
        "term": "Pad"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 139,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:pad",
      "text": "A SAM physical pin, identified by `(group, pin)` (e.g. `(0, 23)` = PA23). Distinct from \"GPIO\" in the ESP sense — a SAM pad does not carry an inherent GPIO number; it carries an alternate-function multiplexer."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "SAM D5x/E5x Family Data Sheet §15 Table 15-3.",
        "term": "PCHCTRL channel"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 140,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:pchctrl channel",
      "text": "Per-peripheral generic-clock channel in GCLK. Each peripheral has a fixed PCHCTRL index (e.g. SERCOM0_CORE is channel 7 on D5x); the chip YAML's `peripherals.<name>.gclk_pchctrl_id:` key records it. Required for SERCOM / TC / TCC / ADC / DAC; not required for AHB-only blocks like NVMCTRL."
    },
    {
      "attrs": {
        "relationship": "This doc; mirrors ESP.",
        "term": "compile-verify"
      },
      "doc": "chipdb/rlvgl-chips-microchip/docs/CHIPS-MICROCHIP-00-CONCEPTS.md",
      "family": "chips-microchip",
      "kind": "term",
      "line": 141,
      "obj_id": "chips-microchip:term:compile-verify",
      "text": "The opt-in test pattern that materialises a throwaway cargo project around the generated BSP files and runs `cargo check` against the real upstream PAC on `thumbv7em-none-eabihf` (or `thumbv6m-none-eabi`). Encoded by CHIPS-MICROCHIP-NN as `tests/bsp_microchip_compile.rs` behind a `compile-verify` Cargo feature. As defined in `tests/bsp_esp32c3_compile.rs`; adapted: target triple and PAC crate name"
    },
